WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:03.820
The Needle Beetle is a clever device

2
00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:06.820
that allows you to quickly select and

3
00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:10.060
position needles for stitch patterning.

4
00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:12.010
It is specific to the 6.5mm.

5
00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:14.420
or 9mm machines

6
00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:18.980
that don't have automatic patterning
(punch card or electronics).

7
00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:25.460
Here are some facts the beetle will
repeat any 8stitch pattern repeat.

8
00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:28.060
It only works from right to left.

9
00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:29.780
Don't try to force it the other

10
00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:32.940
way. To use it

11
00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.940
you set up your stitch pattern over

12
00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:37.780
the first 8 needles.

13
00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:40.120
Use the beetle and the pattern repeat will

14
00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:44.020
be duplicated across all
the needles in work.

15
00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:47.100
The selected needles end up in "D" position.

16
00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:49.780
Ready for stitch patterning
determined by your.

17
00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:53.620
Carriage settings like slip and tuck.

18
00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:56.260
Use the Knit it Now Cheat Sheets to make

19
00:00:56.290 --> 00:00:58.580
it easire to set up complicated stitch.

20
00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:02.220
Patterns, let's do a very simple example.

21
00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:07.980
First, we have some needles in work
working over the first eight needles

22
00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:14.490
on the right of the needles in work, align
the needles for every other needle set up.

23
00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:21.740
Skip the first needle and put needles 2,
4, 6 and 8 into "C" position.

24
00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:23.820
Now you don't have to be exact.

25
00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:30.210
Notice the indicator on the needle bed
where the "C" position is.

26
00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:32.740
Place the beetle on the needle bed.

27
00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:34.160
If you have a lot of needles

28
00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:36.280
in work, remove the knitting carriage so

29
00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:39.740
you can place the beetle
on the needle bed.

30
00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:45.600
With your hand and your fingers over
the beetle, pass it to the left.

31
00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:48.380
You'll see that every other needle is

32
00:01:48.410 --> 00:01:55.000
being selected and placed
in "D" position across the row.

33
00:01:55.320 --> 00:02:01.000
This is duplicating, that first
8 sequence that you set up.

34
00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:03.210
Here's another example.

35
00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:06.900
This time, put all needles
into working position again.

36
00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:10.170
Skip one needle on the right and pull just

37
00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:14.500
two needles to "C" position
pass the beetle.

38
00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:16.860
You'll see the selected stitch sequence

39
00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:22.420
repeated across the row.
Using the Knit it Now

40
00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:26.890
Cheat Sheets can help make
using the beetle even easier.

41
00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:29.080
The grid is sized exactly for the

42
00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:31.580
needle spacing on your machine.

43
00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:34.300
Just copy the stitch pattern to the grid.

44
00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:39.380
I like to use colored markers and hold
it up to the needle bed row by row.

45
00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:42.860
To select the needles of your design.

46
00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:44.980
You just need to select the first

47
00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:47.340
8 needles and then let the beetle.

48
00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:49.610
Repeat them across the row.

49
00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:52.020
No more counting needles.

50
00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:54.060
There's something to keep in mind.

51
00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:58.020
You probably won't want
to pattern on the end needle.

52
00:02:58.050 --> 00:03:03.260
So you'll want to copy the entire 8
stitches across the row and then return

53
00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:07.480
the end needles to "B" position
so they don't tuck or slip.

